    "AI Notes": {
      "value": "London studio founded 2003 by Kirsty Carter and Emma Thomas; approx 6-7 people. Tagline: creative direction, design and type for culture. Work spans brand identity, editorial, campaigns, packaging, exhibition graphics, signage, digital and web, plus a type foundry (APFEL Type). Clients include Tate, V&A, Barbican, Gagosian, David Zwirner, Aesop, Birkenstock, Hermes (John Lobb). Founders are co-Presidents of AGI UK Chapter; studio described as one of the UK's most influential design studios (source: its nicethat, LinkedIn, Communication Arts). Work Status set as Studio (active operating studio). Instagram confirmed at @apracticeforeverydaylife (25K followers, 419 posts, handle verified via their own About page). Email n@apracticeforeverydaylife.com is confirmed genuine: their About page lists two single-letter addresses (n@ for new business, m@ for general enquiries); intentional studio convention, not a truncation error.",
